{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Blocked/residual semantic finding after Gerrit CL 2626 landed: the patchset-2 `_dc_support.py` migration from legacy `--filter-local-ids` to primary `--only` is not semantically equivalent for the live Jira DC inbound-create leg. `pass_support.resolve_selection()` resolves `--only` tokens only to existing local ticket ids or existing bindings (`bindings.get_local_id(token)`) and reports unresolved tokens otherwise; `load_phase` then calls `ensure_selection_current()` before narrowing inputs. For a not-yet-bound inbound Jira issue, neither the derived local id nor raw Jira key exists in local_tickets/bindings yet, so `sync --only <local_id>,<key>` can fail before the differ sees the inbound create. The removed post-filter path instead seeded `_build_filter_target_set()` with tokens verbatim and matched mutation `target`/`provenance.jira_key` after the full differ, so the raw Jira key could scope the inbound create. Per orchestrator instruction, this is a design escalation rather than a mechanical harness migration. Related citations: `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_support.py` `resolve_selection`, `ensure_selection_current`, `narrow_selection_inputs`, `_build_filter_target_set`; `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/load_phase.py` selection resolution/narrowing; `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_phase.py` post-filter behavior; `tests/external/live_jira_dc/_dc_fixtures.py` and `test_store_copy_isolation.py` comments documenting the inbound-create key+local-id requirement."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788550502223478646,"uuid":"9bc960cc-cd1f-4851-bf72-8ca8494efbf8"}